Compatible display for older car browsers (2026-10-17). A tester's Tesla on Chrome 113 decoded every frame - fps
full, no error - and showed nothing: the low-latency canvas (desynchronized, playport-latency.patch) and the
hardware-decoder preference (prefer-hardware) failed there without an error, and both fall back only on one (the
watchdog only waits for the first decoded frame). Compatible display uses neither: about one frame later, the
browser picks the decoder. On by default below Chrome 120, the oldest car browser seen working (XPeng G6; the
Tesla we drove runs 148); a switch in Display turns it on or off for that browser and reloads the page. The
viewer log carries compat=0/1 next to chrome.

